: "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": "320pq2"}, {"n": 6, "text": "A rare book dealer sells a vintage novel to a collector for ₹1,440. The collector later auctions it at a 25% profit. What price does the final buyer pay at the auction?", "options": [{"text": "₹1,620", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,860", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,800", "added": false}, {"text": "₹360", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": "₹1,800"}, {"n": 7, "text": "The amount on a sum of ₹6,400 at the rate of 15% per annum compound interest, compounded annually, in 2 years will be:", "options": [{"text": "₹8,375", "added": false}, {"text": "₹8,078", "added": false}, {"text": "₹8,413", "added": false}, {"text": "₹8,464", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-formula", "key_answer": "₹8,464"}, {"n": 8, "text": "The average of the first 12 odd natural numbers is:", "options": [{"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "12.5", "added": false}, {"text": "11.5", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "12"}, {"n": 9, "text": "611", "options": [{"text": "1848 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "1798 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "1978 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "2048 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "other", "key_answer": "1848 cm2"}, {"n": 10, "text": "Shivam spends 50% of his income. If he saves ₹42,000, then his income (in ₹) is:", "options": [{"text": "83,000", "added": false}, {"text": "85,000", "added": false}, {"text": "21,000", "added": false}, {"text": "84,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": "84,000"}, {"n": 11, "text": "Find the median for the data 9, 6, 8, 11, 16, and 22.", "options": [{"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Elementary Statistics", "sub": "mean-median-mode", "key_answer": "10"}, {"n": 12, "text": "What is the minimum value that must be assigned to A so that the 8-digit number 322A4828 is divisible by 4?", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": "0"}, {"n": 13, "text": "If the marked price of a fan is ₹775 and a discount of 12% is given on it, then what is the selling price of the fan?", "options": [{"text": "₹682", "added": false}, {"text": "₹686", "added": false}, {"text": "₹680", "added": false}, {"text": "₹684", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "₹682"}, {"n": 14, "text": "Three workers, A, B, and C, are assigned to paint a wall. A can complete the task in 8 hours, B in 12 hours, and C in 16 hours. If they all start together but C leaves after 2 hours, how much time in total will it take to finish the task?", "options": [{"text": "3 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "5.5 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "4.2 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "6 hours", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "4.2 hours"}, {"n": 15, "text": "The population of a village was 1,60,000. It increased by 15% in the first year and increased by 30% in the second year. Its population after two years will be _______.", "options": [{"text": "2,08,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,84,000", "added": false}, {"text": "2,39,200", "added": false}, {"text": "2,32,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "population-and-depreciation", "key_answer": "2,39,200"}, {"n": 16, "text": "Suman, Tariq and Neha invest sums in the ratio 6 : 11 : 12, respectively. If they earned a total profit of ₹79,721 at the end of the year, then what is the positive difference between the shares of Suman and Neha?", "options": [{"text": "₹16,492", "added": false}, {"text": "₹16,493", "added": false}, {"text": "₹16,494", "added": false}, {"text": "₹16,491", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "partnership", "key_answer": "₹16,494"}, {"n": 17, "text": "In a race, an athlete covers a distance of 450 m in 150 sec in the first lap. He covers the second lap of the same distance in 75 sec. What is the average speed (in m/sec) of the athlete?", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": "4"}, {"n": 18, "text": "Amit can do a piece of work in 13 days. Gopal is 30% more efficient than Amit. The number of days taken by Gopal to do the same piece of work is:2972", "options": [{"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "10"}, {"n": 19, "text": "If the length of a rectangle is 5 cm more than the breadth and if the perimeter of the rectangle is 40 cm, then the length and breadth of the rectangle will be: Ans A. B. C. D.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": "D"}, {"n": 20, "text": "In an election between two candidates, 78% of the voters cast their votes, out of which 4% votes were declared invalid. A candidate got 13,572 votes, out of which 58% were valid votes. Find the total number of voters enrolled in that election.", "options": [{"text": "33,540", "added": false}, {"text": "31,250", "added": false}, {"text": "30,150", "added": false}, {"text": "28,680", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": "31,250"}, {"n": 21, "text": "A retailer offers the following discount schemes for buyers on an article. Which scheme will fetch the maximum selling price?", "options": [{"text": "Two successive discounts of 10%", "added": false}, {"text": "Successive discounts of 25% and 36%", "added": false}, {"text": "A discount of 12% followed by a discount of 46%", "added": false}, {"text": "A discount of 23% followed by a discount of 15%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": "Two successive discounts of 10%"}, {"n": 22, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "556.375 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "606.375 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "506.475 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "616.475 cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "other", "key_answer": "606.375 cm3"}]}